{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars","id":1241128,"title":"Canon Usurpation Surviving Solars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-31T19:49:42-07:00","id":1241128,"title":"Canon Usurpation Surviving Solars","content":"Hi, I make this topic to discuss and see if someone has a list, or knows of, solars who survived the usurpation , this doesn't mean first age survivors, but those exaltation shards that escaped the Jade prison.<br /> The ones I know about are:<br /> The Nexus Emisary, in one of the possible background choices for him in MoTD Scavenger Lands.<br /> Filial Wisdom, the 200 years old Solar who became Han Ta's servant, in MoTD The East<br /> One of the incarnations of thrice damned Gorol is supposed to have survived the usurpation hiding in Malfeas, In MoEP Infernals.<br /> A Dawn caste was supposed to be a survivor in the North and had deals with demons to have revenge, I think he appears in MoTD The North, he may or not be the Bull.<br /> The Bull of the North Kaneko, is supposed to be a solar exaltation that survived. <br /> I'm not sure but I think <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Samea of the Blackwater tribe is also one of the surviving exaltations, I don't remember where but I think of reading that she joined Kaneko before the solars were freed from the jade prison. </span></span><br /> I've heard rumors that one of the incarnations of the creator of the Devil Tiger style , survived in a chrysalis, being the actual Devil Tiger.<br /> <br /> So anyone knows of any other ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 07-31-2018, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:58:54-07:00","id":1241134,"title":"","content":"You mean Righteous Devil, not Devil Tiger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:50:11-07:00","id":1241165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars#post1241128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I make this topic to discuss and see if someone has a list, or knows of, solars who survived the usurpation , this doesn't mean first age survivors, but those exaltation shards that escaped the Jade prison.<br /> The ones I know about are:<br /> The Nexus Emisary, in one of the possible background choices for him in MoTD Scavenger Lands.<br /> Filial Wisdom, the 200 years old Solar who became Han Ta's servant, in MoTD The East<br /> One of the incarnations of thrice damned Gorol is supposed to have survived the usurpation hiding in Malfeas, In MoEP Infernals.<br /> A Dawn caste was supposed to be a survivor in the North and had deals with demons to have revenge, I think he appears in MoTD The North, he may or not be the Bull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deret Khan, who fathered the apheliotropes (originally in a web enhancement for Creatures of the Wyld). He was probably not the predecessor of the Bull of the North.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bull of the North Kaneko, is supposed to be a solar exaltation that survived.<br /> I'm not sure but I think <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Samea of the Blackwater tribe is also one of the surviving exaltations, I don't remember where but I think of reading that she joined Kaneko before the solars were freed from the jade prison. </span></span><br /> I've heard rumors that one of the incarnations of the creator of the Devil Tiger style , survived in a chrysalis, being the actual Devil Tiger.<br /> <br /> So anyone knows of any other ? </div> </div> </div>First edition actually had Yurgen and co being from recently-released Exaltations back in the Dawnbook. The introduction of Joachim and his presentation may have tripped suspicions that the two were related, both being Icewalker Solars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T22:01:48-07:00","id":1241169,"title":"","content":"Samea is even older than the Bull. So far as 2E told us, minus the Goblin King, she's the oldest of the living Solars. I would SURMISE that Mirror Flag is either one of the very first of the returning Solars, or (more likely) just a little bit older, and belongs to the &quot;Persistent 20.&quot; She's seen already fairly confident in her abilities, but willing to accept help from Ayesha Uru and her Golds on her own terms in 1E Sidereals. The &quot;Gold Faction&quot; was in its uttermost infancy in that comic, and the timeline for CotI doesn't really mesh with that notion well.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Righteous Devil&quot; found in the crystal coffin there's no way to know. Given how his legend plays in the South, he might've laid down in that box last week.<br /> <br /> Edit: Was there ever even 100% confirmation Joachim was a Solar?<br /> Double Edit: If you're just interested in the Exaltations of the Persistent 20, CoCD: Underworld or a variety of other sources (Including Oadanel's Codex, which covers the Invisible Manse survivors and their fate) talk about Kal Bax and the other Solars who escaped the Massacre, but eventually died (or were murdered at the behest of the gone-insane Intelligence of the Invisible Manse) in the Invisible Manse. What *I* want to know, is how did the Green Lady confirm their deaths, BEFORE the known ascension of the Deathlords? Kind of makes you wonder just how long that quadruple-traitor has been screwing around with the Deathlords, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 08-01-2018, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T03:33:03-07:00","id":1241231,"title":"","content":"In Arms there's mention of a solar who survived the usurpation with help from his sidereal sister. He died a few centuries later, trying to take revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:53:18-07:00","id":1241285,"title":"","content":"This topic always amuses me, I'm patiently waiting for when we reach the point where the numbers can be used to tell us that the Calibration Massacre didn't actually kill a single Solar (obviously by this point all 100 Sidereals will have died in the attack, in some cases repeatedly) and that the Jade Prison is propaganda to hide the fact that they collectively moped around for over a thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-01-2018, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:09:52-07:00","id":1241291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1241285#post1241285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic always amuses me, I'm patiently waiting for when we reach the point where the numbers can be used to tell us that the Calibration Massacre didn't actually kill a single Solar (obviously by this point all 100 Sidereals will have died in the attack, in some cases repeatedly) and that the Jade Prison is propaganda to hide the fact that they collectively moped around for over a thousand years.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication was that there were 10-20ish solars who escaped. So it's not hard to see a few people who escaped. The fact that more than a few sidereals die each time is dumb. Especially when they note them as elder sidereals because at this point it sounds like kejak and h8s crew have been dead ten tikes over. <br /> <br /> I think the one who always interested me was the one who left to slay demons in malfeas, way back in the first age, and still is implied to be alive today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T19:14:44-07:00","id":1241626,"title":"","content":"If you want to get into silly with 2E:<br /> The utter SILENCE on how not even ONE Solar managed to come into enough power to require a major Sidereal intervention during a) The NUMEROUS, and often highly destructive military-backed regime-changes of the Shogunate (I've found mention of six distinct wars fought internally during &quot;the Shogunate&quot;) and b) The utter upheaval and death of the GC + BC.<br /> <br /> Not ONE Solar Exalted among the Forest People, in the Eastern Bordermarches. Not ONE among the handful of Dune People survivors of the BC. NO Solar Exaltation EVER found meaningful root despite the Sidereals being swamped just trying to handle the Godswar, described as nearly polarizing itself as the Usurpation. No explanation at all why, none of the Persistent 20 got off the ground.<br /> <br /> Edit: For that matter, we get all these &quot;They're cut off, and no one even knows they exist&quot; populations. Luthe, the Saigoth survivors, Tzatli refugees. How many times were the Persistent 20 recycled in 1800 years, anyways? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 08-01-2018, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T22:57:39-07:00","id":1241691,"title":"","content":"Well, what, 12, 14 of those were hiding in the Invisible Fortress. That's most of them. The number outside was tiny.<br /> <br /> But saying that, it might well have happened. There's very little written in the gameline about anything much that happened in the Shogunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T13:42:44-07:00","id":1243586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1241626#post1241626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: For that matter, we get all these &quot;They're cut off, and no one even knows they exist&quot; populations. Luthe, the Saigoth survivors, Tzatli refugees. How many times were the Persistent 20 recycled in 1800 years, anyways? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most of those cut off locations are stable points of creation but are outside of creation, it's fair to assume solar exaltations can't go into the wyld and look for that lost first age city, or all the way into the Underworld to catch a worthy human. Plus most people who gets solar Exaltation are people with big destinies, I doubt that the guys trying to not be sucked dry in Saigoth have much more destiny than we survive another day, IF they have ANY destiny at all, since they are not in the Loom of Fate.<br /> <br /> As for the solars, I would say that most of them were either killed a few weeks after exalting, or managed to get into another realm to hide for a while until they got killed, some of them may have lasted for a few decades even getting into the 100 years, where he would think of himself powerful enough to attack the shogunate and then got killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-07-2018, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T01:38:13-07:00","id":1243730,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I'm pretty sure the &quot;persistent 20&quot; is fanon.<br /> In 1st and 2nd ed canon, there's, I think, 16? The ones in the Invisible Fortress, +2 Dawns. I can't remember if there was 12 or 14 in the Invisible Fortress, I don't have a copy of that book. (What book was it in?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T02:51:42-07:00","id":1243738,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the Shogunate, even when fractured, had forces that were sufficiently well-equipped that they could overwhelm Solars when appropriately dedicated, and guided by motivated Sidereals. Even if those Solars were remote. The Time of Tumult is predicated on the Realm being fractured, the remains not having the best magic, and the number of fires to put out being so many. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1243730#post1243730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I'm pretty sure the &quot;persistent 20&quot; is fanon.<br /> In 1st and 2nd ed canon, there's, I think, 16? The ones in the Invisible Fortress, +2 Dawns. I can't remember if there was 12 or 14 in the Invisible Fortress, I don't have a copy of that book. (What book was it in?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to round it up to twenty just because it's a nice figure.<br /> <br /> Apart from the Invisible Fortress and the two who made a stand at Rathess, there are generally non-specific references to Solars of the Night Caste that manage to go into hiding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kind of makes you wonder just how long that quadruple-traitor has been screwing around with the Deathlords, eh?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Uh-huh.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T03:53:56-07:00","id":1243750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1241626#post1241626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to get into silly with 2E:<br /> The utter SILENCE on how not even ONE Solar managed to come into enough power to require a major Sidereal intervention during a) The NUMEROUS, and often highly destructive military-backed regime-changes of the Shogunate (I've found mention of six distinct wars fought internally during &quot;the Shogunate&quot;) and b) The utter upheaval and death of the GC + BC.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Shogunate was in many ways a chaotic and destructive period, the system in place for hunting down and killing Anathema worked extremely well. The Realm also managed quite well before the disappearance of the Empress and the return of many more Solars in recent years.<br /> <br /> As for the Contagion/Crusade era, any burgeoning Solar empires that managed to somehow contest both disasters when nobody else could would still have the Defence Grid to contend with at the dawn of the Realm. <br /> <br /> Anyone who had carved out an empire beyond the borders of Creation at that time would have the Hannya to contend with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T08:26:33-07:00","id":1243802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1243730#post1243730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What book was it in?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire first half of <i>Time of Tumult</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T08:33:19-07:00","id":1243804,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Unfortunately I don't have a copy so I can't check how many there were. Never mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T08:45:19-07:00","id":1243807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1243804#post1243804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't check how many there were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twelve: Kal Bax himself (Twilight), his apprentice Ozandus Pal (Twilight), Crinis Proles (Twilight), Larquen Quen (Twilight), Arvika Chas (Zenith), Meherrin (Zenith), Kotor Varos (Night), Daveg Chlurion (Night), Vaznia (Night), Aure Orchester (Eclipse), Iatrixian the Weaver (Eclipse), and Surin of Justice (Eclipse).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1243804#post1243804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, some parts were <i>really</i> neat, but others felt rather lackluster.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, there is genuinely an area described in the module, known as &quot;Wangler's Knob.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-08-2018, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T09:43:36-07:00","id":1243825,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> And I remember them being said to be a mix of Castes, except with no Dawns. But I don't think exact Castes for each person were given? Maybe they were? I do remember there were short descriptions of each.<br /> <br /> I had one of my PCs be the reincarnation of Ozandus Pal, because Ozandus Pal is one of the possible candidates for Walker in Darkness's prior incarnation. He had ended up being the main bad guy, so my plan was that they'd go to the Invisible Fortress, learn that I'chan the Twilight was the reincarnation of Ozandus Pal, get Pal's body, and then the party's necromancer, Thothmet, could use it in a ritual to allow Walker in Darkness to be killed by his reincarnation, ie I'chan.<br /> But then I'chan was accidentally killed by another PC, and I realised that basing your plotline about one particular PC is a bit risky. And so they never went there.<br /> <br /> Another of my friends did actually run the module back in 1st ed, with his Dragonblood party. They got there, realised how deadly it was, stole a whole bunch of orichalcum doorknobs from the first few corridors, and then just went home and sold them for fat cash, rather than risking a Solar-made dungeon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAlso, there is genuinely an area described in the module, known as &quot;Wangler's Knob.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I don't see the problem. Presumably it's a hill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T09:53:44-07:00","id":1243828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1243825#post1243825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't think exact Castes for each person were given? Maybe they were?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were indeed. I'll go ahead and edit them into the posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1243825#post1243825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the problem. Presumably it's a hill?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Wang&quot; and &quot;knob&quot; are also slang for &quot;penis.&quot; I have yet to say it out loud <i>once</i> without <i>someone</i> laughing. &gt;.&gt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T11:38:29-07:00","id":1243859,"title":"","content":"Alucard! I'm shocked! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How could you interpret such a thing as rude!<br /> <br /> Next you'll be saying good British place names like Sandy Balls, Shitterton, Cockshoot Close, Dick Court, etc are rude.<br /> <br /> I think the real dirty-minded person isn't the writer, it's you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T11:42:49-07:00","id":1243864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1243807#post1243807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twelve: Kal Bax himself (Twilight), his apprentice Ozandus Pal (Twilight), Crinis Proles (Twilight), Larquen Quen (Twilight), Arvika Chas (Zenith), Meherrin (Zenith), Kotor Varos (Night), Daveg Chlurion (Night), Vaznia (Night), Aure Orchester (Eclipse), Iatrixian the Weaver (Eclipse), and Surin of Justice (Eclipse).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so canonically we've got 2 Dawns (Yurgen+Filial Wisdom's ancestors), 4 Twilights, 2 Zeniths*, 3 Eclipses, and those 3 Nights plus a handful of others who were mentioned to escape.<br /> <br /> *In the modern day, Samea is a Zenith who exalted before the destruction of the Jade Prison, but she could be the reincarnation of Arvika Chas or Meherrin.<br /> <br /> 20 in total is probably reasonable, but it could be lower if you wanted.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, something else I was thinking about. In 3rd ed, the Solars stopped exalting for two different reasons; 1)The Jade Prison, and 2)The Unconquered Sun turning his face away.<br /> The exact mechanics of how those interact haven't quite been explained.<br /> <br /> But, I wonder, if 20-ish Solars escaped the Usurpation, whether when they died they reincarnated, but much slower than usual. So after Larquen Quen died alone and insane, rather than a new Twilight just popping up, there might have been a gap of a few years. And after that guy got punked by the Wyld Hunt, another few years before the Exaltation was given to a new host. And when she was finally caught and decapitated by the Wyld Hunt, there was another few years' gap.<br /> The reason being that the UCS was exalting slower than usual.<br /> I'm not sure if that'd be good for the game or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-08-2018, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T16:52:42-07:00","id":1243974,"title":"","content":"I feel that level of resolution would be detrimental to the game.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, did anyone else feel the refuge carved out under the Invisible Fortress was too long? Like, given the chance to edit it myself, I feel like I would've cut out about half to two-thirds of those rooms. Even ignoring how it feels a little too large and elaborate to represent a hiding place dug out by a desperate crafter whose resources were dwindling, it just feels like exploring it to its end in-game would take frustrating amounts of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T11:22:33-07:00","id":1246709,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2093_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2093\" data-vbnamecard=\"2093\">Crumplepunch</a> Why would a Solar need to &quot;survive&quot; the GC or BC? The 20 free Solar Exaltations just keep Re-Exalting individuals among the tiny percentage of survivors until both events stopped killing mortals, and as soon as the Balorian Crusade was beaten back by the Realm Defense Grid, there would've been 20 fresh Solar Exalts on the ground...Just as the Empress was damaging the Blessed Isle blasting her Dragon Blooded rivals who refused to submit.<br /> <br /> Right at that moment, look at CoCD: Yu-Shan for a look at what shambles Heaven was in by the end of the Fair Folk invasion. What remained of the divine Terrestrial hierarchy then was so hostile to the Celestial divinities and Heaven they were attacking any Heavenly agents not accompanied by multiple celestial lions...the Godswar was a huge mess, and Heaven had JUST been FLOODED by all the now-unemployed deities the BC had created.<br /> <br /> Into that mess, one could easily imagine a Solar or two managing to get a foothold. If a simple Wyld Hunt failure immediately prior to the Empress's disappearance could result in the Bull, how much more easily could something similar have happened during that larger disaster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T11:38:56-07:00","id":1246713,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was, and the Realm crushed them 20 years later.<br /> It's probably worth mentioning that Yurgen didn't beat the Tepet legions by himself. He got lucky: out of the 20-ish Solars in the whole world, 2 exalted amongst the Icewalkers. They joined each other, started building their power far from the Realm, and then when the other Solars returned recruited 3 of them (though one died fighting the Tepets). <br /> That's not something likely to happen shortly after the GC, it'd be probably just 1 Solar.<br /> <br /> Frankly, compared to 400 Lunars, pretty irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Crumplepunch didn't actually say Solars needed to survive, they said &quot;burgeoning Solar Empires&quot;. A brand new Solar isn't nearly as dangerous as the experienced old Night Caste who just died of the Great Contagion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-16-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T08:16:26-07:00","id":1247025,"title":"","content":"Huh. I always heard 30, not twenty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T00:27:36-07:00","id":1249073,"title":"","content":"2nd ed had Sun Dragon a Solar who went to live in Malfeas picking fights. The developers mentioned it\u2019s possible he could have devolved primordial charms or something weird like that, I forget.<br /> <br /> <br /> In my headcanon Queen M-r-l survives the Usrpation and was weary with ennui so the Sidereals parlayed with her and she agreed to retire to her city sized tomb as a living Ancestor that everyone agrees to to treat as legally dead.<br /> <br /> I also have it that a few Solar schemers independently believe they came up with the Usurpation and helped keep it a secret from behind the scenes but because they didn\u2019t know about each other their schemes helped kill each other. Except for one who shunted off into the Wyld on a floating continent to reverse engineer their own Prinordial from powerful spirits and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T01:30:10-07:00","id":1249078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1241128-canon-usurpation-surviving-solars?p=1247025#post1247025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I always heard 30, not twenty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 14 confirmed for definite, probably a bit higher. I think any number from 15-30 is reasonable. I'd personally say 30 is a bit high, but it could be appropriate for a game.<br /> To be honest, it's probably not something that's good to stamp in stone. I'd prefer a lower reason, but it needs to be a bit flexible in case someone wants to run a Solar game in the year 400RY or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}